 "unreadable": [
  "Slashed zeros read as 0 (e.g. P0.13, P1.08, D0/TX)"
 ],
 "notes": "Labels use the nRF52840 port name (P0.xx/P1.xx) where printed, else the board/power name. Functions read outward from the pin. Power-direction tags (IN/OUT), 'D' default icons and LED icons omitted; RESET overbar not representable. Image 1 is the gen-1 Nano 33 BLE style pinout (MISO/MOSI, RX/TX); images 2-3 print CIPO/COPI and D1/RX, D0/TX. Skipped: LED callouts (BUILT_IN LED, Power), bottom-view callouts pointing at a few header pads (~D8/~D7 NFC, +3V3/GND battery jumper, +5V/VBUS jumper) since no full row map is given."
}
